  "limitations": "Inputs MUST be UT1, not an assumed UTC timestamp. No UT1-UTC lookup, IERS data, polar motion, sidereal-time model, nutation, observer coordinates or full Earth-orientation transform. The schema only bounds numerical values; it cannot prove a timescale label is correct. Very remote epochs can lose numerical/model accuracy despite being inside the arithmetic bounds.",
  "port_notes": "Ports eraEra00 with ordering of the two date parts, t=d1+(d2-J2000), fractional parts using C-style fmod, the exact IAU constants and eraAnp normalization. Degrees are a derived convenience output. This is a separate Earth-rotation primitive, not a generic 3D rotation pack and not the earlier solar-position algorithm. Full ERFA source notices remain intact.",
